course: dictionary
lesson: 4427
title: Names in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names, and a name often starts with a capital letter. Han is one of them. Its meaning depends on the words around it. «China was ruled by dynasties, families whose rule passed from parent to child, such as the Shang, Zhou, Qin, Han, Tang, Song and Ming.» Here Han is one of the dynasties, the families who ruled China.
explain: A name can point to a family, a people, a river, a language or a person. Read the words next to it for clues. «Han Chinese are the largest ethnic group in China and in the world» tells you Han names a people. «Han Solo» from «Star Wars» is a person, because Solo is a surname and the story is about people.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «Hànzì» pupils meet in Mandarin lessons, Hànzì means Chinese characters, so the writing still makes sense. If your meaning fits, you are probably right. If it does not, look up the word in a dictionary.
fact: Han is a name, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «The Han dynasty» means a family of emperors who ruled China for about four hundred years.
fact: «Han Chinese» means the largest ethnic group in China and in the world.
fact: «Hànzì» means Chinese characters, and «Hànyǔ» means the Chinese language.
fact: Han is also a Korean family name, a river in Korea, and a first name, as in Han Solo from «Star Wars».
exercise: «China was ruled by dynasties, such as the Shang, Zhou, Qin, Han, Tang, Song and Ming.» In this sentence, what is Han? | A kind of Chinese writing | An inn for travellers | A river in Seoul | *One of the dynasties that ruled China
exercise: In Mandarin lessons pupils meet «Hànzì». What does Hànzì mean? | A Korean family name | *Chinese characters | A river in Seoul | A Chinese emperor
exercise: Ellie hears about «Han Solo» in «Star Wars». What kind of word is Han here? | *A first name, the name of a person in a film | A Chinese river | An inn for travellers | A dynasty of emperors
test: «Han Chinese are the largest ethnic group in China and in the world.» What does Han Chinese mean? | A Korean river | A kind of paper | A small village in Turkey | *The largest ethnic group in China and the world
test: «A han was an inn for travellers in Turkey and the Middle East.» What is a han? | *An inn for travellers | A famous castle | A kind of Chinese emperor | A river in Korea
exam: Pupil asks, «How do I know if Han with a capital H is a person, a family or a place?» What is the best answer? | Capital letters always mean a river | The words around it and the capital letter show it is a name, so check which kind of name it is | *Ignore the words around it and guess | Skip it and never look at it again
